 "transcript": {
  "answer": "The RBA's cash rate target is about **4.35%**. The most recent monthly average is **4.36% (September 2026)**, so the rate has held at roughly that level since June 2026.\n\nThe rate has risen from 3.60% in January 2026. The monthly averages show increases from February through May, then a plateau:\n\n- Jan 2026: 3.60%\n- Mar 2026: 3.96%\n- May 2026: 4.31%\n- Jun to Sep 2026: about 4.35%\n\nInflation explains the tightening. In August 2026 the trimmed mean (the RBA's preferred underlying measure) was **3.6% year-on-year**, up from 2.8% in June 2025. Headline CPI was **4.0%** year-on-year in August 2026. Both are above the RBA's 2–3% target band.\n\nI don't have the exact meeting dates or the Board's latest statement, so check the RBA's website for its current stance and any decision after September.",
